THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL DISTRIBUTED WITH THIS REPOSITORY

4. part-one/realinho2022_students.csv is a curated subset of the student
   records released as "Predict Students' Dropout and Academic Success" in the
   UCI Machine Learning Repository (dataset 697) by Realinho, V., Machado, J.,
   Baptista, L., and Martins, M. V. (2022). Predicting student dropout and
   academic success. Data, 7(11), 146.
   https://doi.org/10.3390/data7110146 — licensed CC BY 4.0. That attribution
   and licence travel with the file and with any redistribution of it.

5. part-one/galton1886_sons.csv (Chapter 7): Galton's family heights
   (published 1886), transcribed by J. A. Hanley and distributed in the R
   package HistData under the GPL; one son per family drawn for QMSBR. The
   measurements are historical records in the public domain; the extract is
   redistributed with this attribution.
   https://doi.org/10.32614/CRAN.package.HistData

6. The embedded secondary-school example data used in Chapter 2 are curated subsets
   derived from Cortez, P. (2008). Student Performance. UCI Machine Learning
   Repository.
   https://doi.org/10.24432/C5TG7T — licensed CC BY 4.0. That attribution and
   licence travel with the file and with any redistribution of it.

7. apa.csl comes from the Citation Style Language styles collection and is
   licensed CC BY-SA 3.0. It credits Brenton M. Wiernik, Andrew Dunning, the
   CSL styles collection, and the Style Variant Builder.
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

8. Everything under practice/ — the R-support pages, the bundled Quarto
   Live/WebR runtime under practice/site_libs/, and the data files under
   practice/data/ — keeps its own sources and terms, which are stated in
   practice/LICENSE and in the data note those pages link to.

The PDF sources also use koma_heading_tags.tex, adapted from the KOMA-Script
project's heading-hook example based on code by Ulrike Fischer. Its source
attribution is retained in the file. This third-party adaptation is not
represented as original QMSBR R code under item 2 above.
https://sourceforge.net/p/koma-script/wiki-en/HowTo_Tagging/

THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL NOT DISTRIBUTED HERE

9. Package datasets used in examples — including carData::Baumann,
   carData::Prestige, and AER::STAR — are loaded from their R packages and are
   not redistributed by QMSBR. They retain their own terms; the chapters cite
   the packages and the original studies.

10. Bootstrap, search, font, and related assets that Quarto generates during a
    build retain their upstream licences. They are build outputs, not QMSBR code.

11. Citing a work does not license it. External names and trademarks remain the
